From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:06:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/56] Session restore: periodic snapshots off the UI thread

While edits come in, a snapshot is due 2 s after typing pauses and at the
latest 15 s after the first edit not yet saved, so continuous typing is
still saved and a crash loses about 2 s, 15 s at worst. No snapshot
without edits; unchanged drafts are not rewritten.

The text is copied on the UI thread; hashing, writing and fsync run in a
blocking task, one snapshot at a time under the store's lock. Each
snapshot carries a generation: an older one is skipped by the store and
its result ignored. A failed write keeps the old hash, so quit writes
again synchronously and asks to save if it still fails. Cleanup never
deletes a draft the running snapshot writes, and a snapshot queued
before restore was switched off writes nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

